														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841607">
									

<p>Hello there!<br />
Interesting SCP You've got there! Would be a shame if someone&#8230;<br />
Critiqued it&#8230;.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Overall, I'm thinking this is a relatively solid base concept, but there are a few places your concept falls flat:</p>
<ul>
<li>Tropes: This concept is falling into the standard a-<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/things-what-do-a-thing-an-essay-on-things">thing-that-does-a-thing trope</a>, in this case, a computer that teleports people. That isn't enough to have a solid SCP. It doesn't have anything that distinguishes it from other SCPs. You need something that expands on that idea, more than just anomalous abilities. You need a story too hook your reader in and keep them there, and that's where my next point comes in.</li>
<li>Central narrative: My primary concern is that there simply isn't enough detail being put into your story, which is <strong>the most important part of the entire article</strong>. SCPs have evolved beyond simple items. You don't need to go overboard with our story. Exploration logs are a good start, but you need to go beyond that. Give me some specifics about them. Why can the computer teleport people into the images? How do the images appear? Are the images physical locations? Who goes into the painting? You mention an MTF unit, but what makes them so special? Is there a specific individual that the story revolves around?</li>
<li>Conciseness: Your story is a bit all over the place. You have an interview, a hostile group, an MTF unit, and seemingly no way that all those events are associated with each other. You want to simplify your base concept as much as possible, and then expand on the finer details. It may take a bit of thinking, but once you get that idea, you've struck gold, and the potential is endless.</li>
<li>Attention-Grabber: What is going to make your SCP different from others? Plenty of SCPs have &quot;differing landscapes&quot; and &quot;recurring characters&quot;. What is different about yours? What makes yours unique? Tell me why your audience should read YOUR article, rather than another article.</li>
</ul>
<p>Best of luck with this SCP, and please do PM me if you would like me to take another look! Great job thus far, and with a bit of effort, I think this concept is going to go a long way!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

